    "id": "thm:fixed-nuisance-marked-pair",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "There exist \\(c>0\\) and \\(P_{0,n},P_{1,n}\\in\\mathcal M\\) with the same \\(p_x\\), the same \\(f_x=f^{\\circ}\\), and the same two fixed nonidentical asymmetric error laws, such that \\(Y\\mid(A=a,X=x)\\) is Bernoulli under both laws, \\(\\|\\mu_{1,n}-\\mu_{0,n}\\|_{L^\\infty(I)}\\ge c r_n\\), and \\(\\|P_{1,n,\\mathrm{obs}}^{\\otimes n}-P_{0,n,\\mathrm{obs}}^{\\otimes n}\\|_{\\mathrm{TV}}\\le\\eta\\) for all sufficiently large \\(n\\).",
